!! me-id: amicr039
!   MicroEmacs - History
## HISTORY


  This version of MicroEmacs is based on an early _MicroEmacs_ release of 3.8
  in 1988, the origins of which are unknown, except to say it was delivered
  on a unmarked 5 1/2 floppy disk.

  The program was originally ported to a Motorola MVME147 UNIX box as an
  alternative to __vi__. Reliability of the program proved to be a problem as it
  constantly crashed. In an attempt to rectify the problems the development
  of MicroEmacs commenced.

  Development has continued from 1988 through to today, on the whole
  oblivious to further developments of the existing __MicroEmacs__ program. This
  was due to no Internet access. It was not until 1996 the next version of
  __MicroEmacs__ and __mewin__ (Microsoft Windows (TM) port of the same program) was
  downloaded from the Internet and compared. By this time MicroEmacs was
  radically different and we were not about to mesh the two together - that
  would be a step backwards.

  Development of MicroEmacs has been biased towards the UNIX platform, as
  most of the early development was performed in the UNIX domain. The first
  of the window servers was X-Windows, which in turn has shaped the
  implementation of the Microsoft Windows port. Latterly, we have seen the
  resurgence of the IBM-PC platform which is now commonplace. For the return
  port to the DOS environment, and subsequent development of the Microsoft
  Windows port, a UNIX like interface was required. Most existing users
  could not abide the primitive editors found on these machines; Microsoft
  Windows was an alien and hostile environment when compared with UNIX.
  Hence, the MicroEmacs interface utilizes UNIX style cut and paste across
  all platforms.

  For portability, MicroEmacs utilizes character rendering on all platforms
  regardless of the window manager. Under X-Windows and Microsoft Windows,
  the display is still treated as a character based display, the subtle
  difference is that the display pane is re-sizable. This means that the
  scroll bars, fonts etc. are not as slick as they could be, certainly under
  Microsoft Windows MicroEmacs looks positively primitive!! Regardless of
  the look, the goal of a common editor across all working platforms has
  been achieved!


## Development History 

  - [261010] - Release v09.12.26.beta6

  - [261010] - Encoding-aware clipboard and kill ring (ticket 17): kill
               buffer encoding tags survive clipboard round trips,
               copy-out encodes to the target for X selection targets
               and external tools, unmappable characters become \uXXXX
               escapes in single-byte buffers, and the new yank-as
               command re-tags and yanks the kill buffer in a chosen
               encoding; Windows killTextEquals parity keeps
               multi-node kills intact.

  - [261010] - Macro evaluation and token buffers raised from 1KB to
               16KB (meEVALBUF_SIZE_MAX) so large &cat/&rep results,
               function arguments and set-variable values no longer
               truncate; empty-list guards for &lget &lset &lfind
               &llen &ldel which could read past an empty list.

  - [261010] - Fixes and additions: re-entrant screenUpdate crash on
               ConfigureNotify during insert-file (ticket 16), Xft
               underline offset and stale XGCFont gate, UTF-8
               highlight desync, count-words counts UTF-8 characters
               (ticket 15), new character string functions &uleft
               &ulen &umid &uright &usin, macOS installer restored
               for 10.15-14, hkmdview recognizes Windows drive and
               UNC paths.

  - [261003] - Documentation catch-up after the 260929-261001 build and CI
               restructure: AGENTS.md testing and CI sections rewritten
               around tests/test-basics.emf and the 7 testing.yml jobs,
               doc/utf8-encoding.md build commands fixed for the
               makefiles/ move, its status header refreshed (tickets 12
               and 13 closed) and the ChangeLog back-filled.

  - [261001] - CI regression tests extended (UTF-8 Greek round-trip and
               triple nested while/repeat) with assertions in every
               testing.yml job plus a new MSYS2 mintty test job.
               Repository restructure: build makefiles into makefiles/,
               install scripts into bin/, docs and examples into docs/ and
               user/; "32" dropped from the build names (mec32.exe ->
               mec.exe, linux32gcc -> linuxgcc, macos32gcc.gmk ->
               macosgcc.gmk).

  - [260930] - Support three nested !while / !repeat loops (was two), with
               a clear error on the fourth; legacy BDF fonts and the
               bdf-fonts workflow removed; AppImage building reworked for
               Debian/Ubuntu.

  - [260929] - Unified build strategy: the top-level unixgcc.gmk now
               drives Linux, Cygwin and MSYS2 terminal builds
               (auto-detected via uname -o) and the root Makefile became a
               portable platform dispatcher; README shortened with old
               releases archived.

  - [260928] - Fixed the long-line horizontal scroll display (ticket 13)
               and field-verified the font selection dialog availability
               rules (ticket 12 font UI follow-up closed).

  - [260925] - Font selection availability truth table: "Choose Font ..."
               appears only when the toolchain can work (xft + fc-list ->
               FreeType dialog, xfontsel only -> legacy dialog, neither ->
               button omitted with an explanatory message).

  - [260924] - Windows mew full BMP UTF-8 display via ExtTextOutW with a
               WCHAR sideband (meFrameLine.wtext); cygwin libXft support;
               UTF-8 documentation updates.

  - [260923] - Assorted ticket 12 fixes: Xft one-character typing lag,
               special-char GC colors, startup SEGV, FreeType font dialog
               port, core-font Hide and umlaut cursor handling,
               insert-symbol cell rendering, and draining queued UTF-8
               continuation bytes in doOneKey.

  - [260922] - libXft TrueType rendering for mew/mecw behind XFT=1 plus
               legacy core-font umlaut display fixes; documented in
               doc/utf8-encoding.md.

  - [260921] - Encoding-aware insert-symbol dialog and CP850 support
               (src/encoding.c, tests/encodings/tcp850.txt).

  - [260919] - Per-buffer encoding rendering for mixed-encoding sessions
               (each buffer paints via its own bp->encoding) and
               cross-encoding rectangle kill/yank.

  - [260915] - UTF-8 character-aware editing: cursor movement, word
               operations and delete/kill treat multi-byte sequences as
               single characters.

  - [260830] - Two nested !while / !repeat loops (first nesting level) in
               dobuf, with tests in tests/loops/while.emf.

  - [260829] - Search path fixes (current directory excluded, newuser
               wizard .erf lookup in ~/.jasspa), Cygwin/MSYS2 install-test
               fixes and buffer-encoding variable ordering in evar.def.

  - [260828] - Native UTF-8 display core: disLineByteOff byte-offset
               mapping keeps the byte-based meLine structure while painting
               UTF-8 at the correct columns (tests/encodings/tutf8.txt);
               CP437/CP4866 restored and BOM detection tested.

  - [260827] - Luit terminal translation experiment, adding the $encoding
               and $internal-encoding variables (later rejected as lossy -
               see doc/utf8-encoding.md).

  - [260826] - README refresh (asciinema links); version set to
               v09.12.26b6.

  - [260824] - Added mdview navigation history and wiki-style link creation.
               History tracks visited files with Start/Prev/Next navigation.
               History view lists all visited files as clickable links.
               Missing files prompt user to create them (wiki-style).
               Added Help page with key binding reference.
               Added Index/Home links if index.md/home.md exist.
               Added File:filename display in navigation bar.
               Added doc/mdview.md, doc/me-functions.md (ME function cheat sheet).

  - [260823] - Added mdview Markdown viewer browser (Ticket 3).
               New command 'mdview' opens a read-only *mdview* buffer with
               rendered Markdown. Supports headers, bold, italic, inline code,
               links [text](url), blockquotes, horizontal rules, lists, images,
               and strikethrough. Link navigation via Return, Tab/Shift-Tab,
               and mouse click. Relative link resolution from source directory.
               Files: jasspa/macros/hkmdview.emf, jasspa/macros/me.emf

  - [260821] - Fixed Wayland clipboard crash in help browser and macros.
               Separated clipboard from kill-buffer: copy-region now only
               updates kill buffer; new copy-region-clipboard command wraps
               both. Added clexec guard to TTgetClipboard() (GUI and
               console) to prevent clipboard fork during macro execution.

  - [260821] - Added temporary clipboard access on Unix via C-c c (copy),
               C-c x (cut), C-c v (paste). clipboard-temp-operation macro
               temporarily enables clipboard mode, performs the operation,
               then restores the original state. Requires $allow-clip-exec
               variable to bypass clexec guard.

  - [260821] - Fixed X11 clipboard duplication: after explicit copy, mouse
               selection no longer overwrites CLIPBOARD. Added
               CLIP_MOUSE_PENDING flag to route mouse selections to PRIMARY
               only.

  - [260821] - Added clipboard tool availability warnings in user-setup and
               startup when clipboard is enabled but no external tool
               (xclip, wl-copy, pbcopy) is found.

  - [260821] - Consolidated clipboard documentation (x11-clipboard.md,
               wayland-clipboard.md, help-copy-fix.md) into
               clipboard-support.md.

  - [260820] - Adding mecb-update and mecb-update.bat scripts for install
  
  - [260819] - Fixing font install issues.
  
  - [260818] - Release 091226.beta4
  
  - [260813] - Adding msysunix buld for terminal mec with Msys2 path support.
  
  - [260811] - Scheme Nord added.

  - [260807] - Fixed terminal resize crash: WINDOW_BUFFER_SIZE_EVENT handler
               now uses meFrameChangeWidth/meFrameChangeDepth for proper
               bounds checking and buffer reallocation. Added pipe mode guard
               for GetConsoleScreenBufferInfo via CONOUT$.

  - [260807] - Fixed user-setup edituser checkbox: corrected index from 11
               to 10 so the "Edit" checkbox toggles the correct registry
               key (/history/edituser). Changed &reg default from "1" to
               "0" so user.emf is not opened by default when unchecked.

  - [260807] - Added mouse support for Windows terminal version (mec32.exe).
               Seems to work on cmd, Powershell and Even Msys2 mintty terminals.
               Native Win32 MOUSE_EVENT for console mode, SGR VT mouse via
               stdin/stdout for pipe mode (mintty). Supports click, drag,
               and scroll wheel. ENABLE_EXTENDED_FLAGS added to console mode.

  - [260804] - support  for  xsel,  xclip  (X11),  wl-copy  (Wayland),  pbpaste
               (MacOS),  clip.exe  (Cygwin-Windows,  WSL-Windows and Windows for
               copying text as well from the terminal to the System clipboard.
               Needs to be enabled within the user-setup dialog.

  - [260801] - fixing pydoc/pydoc3 issue for py-doc macro
  
  - [260731] - adding and documenting @info, @pydoc, @rdoc documentation browser
               startup macros

  - [260729] - adding mouse support for xterm compatible terminals like gnome-terminal or
               the terminal of MacOS using SRG protocoll
               
  - [260518] - Improvements in indentation, formatting and linting Fusion code
  
  - [260505] - Release v09.12.26.beta2, new platform Linux with Kernel 7 Ubuntu intel
            
  - [260417] - Fixing Cut issue not updating  clipboard on X11, fixing selection
               of  primary on Wayland  and the  introduction  of  newlines  with
               wl-paste use in MicroEmacs
  
  - [260415] - Release v09.12.26.beta1, new Platform FreeBSD 15, Cygwin x86 3.3

  - [260412] - Fixing stderr messages with emtpy clipboard
    
  - [260411] - Fixing Windows builds

  - [260410] - Fixed X11 clipboard issue: On X11 (not Wayland), when xclip
               is installed and explicit copy (M-w or C-x C-r) is performed,
               the clipboard is piped through xclip to hand ownership to xclip
               instead of MicroEmacs. This prevents subsequent mouse
               selections from accidentally updating the clipboard. 

  - [260409] - Fixed startup flickering with clipboard enabled. Added CLIP_DISABLED
               check to TTsetClipboard to prevent clipboard operations during startup.
               Changed Wayland clipboard detection to search $PATH for wl-copy/wl-paste
               binaries instead of hardcoded paths. Copy to Wayland clipboard now uses
               background fork to minimize flickering. Fixed X11 clipboard issue: 
               on pure X11 (not Wayland), if xclip is installed, explicit copy
               (M-w or C-x C-r) pipes the clipboard through xclip to hand 
               ownership to xclip, preventing mouse selections from 
               accidentally updating the clipboard. Requires xclip package.
  - [260408] - Fixed Wayland clipboard support: (1) now searches $PATH for
               wl-copy/wl-paste binaries instead of hardcoded /usr/bin paths;
               (2) mouse selection now only uses X11 PRIMARY selection, not
               Wayland clipboard; (3) ESC-w (copy-region) updates both X11
               CLIPBOARD and Wayland clipboard.
  - [260405] - Adding Wayland clipboard support using wl-copy/wl-paste for
               native Wayland apps when running under XWayland or Wayland.
               copy-region (M-w) now updates both X11 CLIPBOARD and Wayland
               clipboard. yank (C-y) tries Wayland first, falls back to X11.
               Mouse selection uses X11 PRIMARY only.
