  __Daniel M. Lawrence - Microemacs V3.8 distribution.__

  Daniel  Lawrence turned  MicroEmacs into an editor for the masses, it is his
  work that  ultimately  made  MicroEmacs so popular.  Daniel did a tremendous
  amount  of  work,  both  adding  features  and  supporting  other  platforms
  resulting in the  MicroEmacs  v3.8 release on which  JASSPA's  MicroEmacs is
  based.

  __Late 1985/early 1986__

  Dave Conroy, the original author, first developed the original code
  base for private use. Various people asked Dave for a copy of the
  program and it was distributed without concern for copyrights or
  ownership as was the custom of that era.


## Work In Progress or Planned 


  Development of MicroEmacs is an on-going process, follows is a list of
  work items which is currently being undertaken or planned:-

  - Horizontal scroll bars.
  - On-line tutorial to help beginners get up and running.
  - Native printer support for the generation of postscript.
  - Inclusion of __zlib(1)__ to allow compressed file reading.


## Release History 


  __2026__
     - Adding CLIPBOARD selection support for X-Windows version (mew) -
       allows copy/paste to work with external applications using Ctrl+C/Ctrl+V.
       Can be enabled via user-setup (Platform page) or $system variable (0x2000000).
     - Adding native UTF-8 and multi-encoding editing - per-buffer
       $buffer-encoding with auto-detection and -E command line override,
       libXft TrueType rendering for mew/mecw (XFT=1) and full BMP display
       in the Windows GUI version (mew). See doc/utf8-encoding.md.
     - Adding an automated regression test suite (tests/test-basics.emf)
       run by GitHub Actions on 7 platform jobs (Linux, macOS, Windows x3,
       Cygwin x2) and three nested !while/!repeat loops.
     - Encoding-aware clipboard and kill ring (ticket 17): copy/paste
       between different encodings round-trips correctly, unmappable
       characters are written as \uXXXX escapes into single-byte
       buffers and the new yank-as command re-tags the kill buffer.
     - Macro evaluation buffers raised from 1KB to 16KB and empty-list
       guards for the &l list functions (&lget &lset &lfind &llen
       &ldel); new character string functions &uleft &ulen &umid
       &uright &usin for UTF-8 aware macro text processing.

